  "contract-validated on every run. A series is {id, family, klass, unit, step_s, segments}: from data_start_ns, each segment",
  "[until_s, [v...]] fills one point per step_s up to until_s (offset from data_start, exclusive), cycling its values; null = no point.",
  "t_alert = data_start + 1320 s; baseline [+120 s, +1200 s), incident [+1200 s, +1800 s). Expected: anomalies.txt and onsets.txt.",
  "What each series exercises: checkout cpu = internal step at t_alert; checkout latency = a ramp from +1330 s that BOCPD moves back;",
  "frontend latency = a step at +1350 s; cart rps = zero-silence from +1380 s (context klass, so an external onset and silent=true);",
  "checkout mem = absence-silence from +1500 s while other metrics go on; payment error_rate = one spike that persistence rejects;",
  "payment mem = noise only. External onsets: checkout (ramp), frontend, cart -> t_onset = the second (second_external)."
